<title>USA: U.S. Nov import prices fell 0.1 pct, Oct rev +0.6.</title>
<headline>U.S. Nov import prices fell 0.1 pct, Oct rev +0.6.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Labor Department report of U.S. import and export price changes by percent (unadjusted).</p>
<p>    -			    Nov    Oct-Rev from  Nov 96/95</p>
<p> ALL IMPORTS		  -0.1    0.6    0.4	1.7</p>
<p> -Petroleum		   -0.1    7.2    6.1     38.3</p>
<p> -Nonpetroleum		-0.2   -0.3   -0.3     -1.9</p>
<p> -Food, Feed, Drink	 -0.6    0.2    0.1     -1.2</p>
<p> -Industrial Supplies	0.1    2.4    2.0	9.7</p>
<p> -Capital Goods	     -0.5   -0.3   -0.3     -3.8</p>
<p> -Motor Vehicles,Parts    -0.2   -0.2   -0.3     -0.3</p>
<p> -Consumer Goods ExAutos  UNCH   -0.2   -0.2     -0.1</p>
<p>Percent changes, not seasonally adjusted --</p>
<p> ALL EXPORTS		  -0.5   -0.2   -0.3     -1.3</p>
<p> -Agricultural		-2.8   -2.7   -2.7     -5.9</p>
<p> -Non-Agricultural	  -0.1    0.1    0.1     -0.7</p>
<p> -Food, Feed, Drink	 -2.6   -3.0   -3.0     -5.9</p>
<p> -Industrial Supplies     -0.5    0.4    0.3     -2.5</p>
<p> -Capital Goods	     UNCH   UNCH   UNCH     -0.2</p>
<p> -Motor Vehicles,Parts     0.2    0.2    0.2	0.5</p>
<p> -Consumer Goods ExAutos  UNCH   UNCH   UNCH	1.2</p>
<p>The department reported November price indexes (1990 base year equals 100) of 108.2 for imports, and 108.0 for exports.</p>
</text>
